 opinion is naturally  escalate tension more efficiently in a  shorter span of time  than pretty much any of the other arcs  climaxing in one of the most anxious  nerve-wracking struggles i've seen from  this series  ever and trust me i'm using the word  struggle in this instance with great  purpose  and utility this wasn't a fight this was  a statement  and luffy i think received that message  loud and clear like to put this into  perspective right  this act was so intensely good and  affected me on such a  cellular level that i for the first time  ever had to tweet out my  thoughts on it before i released this  video heck before i even finished the  script i tweeted that out  my god holy hell this arc was  stupidly good introducing new characters  that reveal so much about the past  a confirmation on a hunch i had from  videos ago that gold roger had to have  handed himself in over to the navy  because he would have been too powerful  receiving breadcrumbs of information  about the world's government that forced  me to put my thinking cap on more than i  was comfortable with in this video but  easily at the forefront of my brain i  have the characters and friends that  i've become deeply attached to over the  last two and a half months and 500  chapters  they are after vanishing and i don't  know where to  but all i do know is that i will be  covering it next week and when i do  i hope you'll be there to join me as  always i've been totally not mark i'll  see you all next week  thank you so much for watching  you
 

